December 20, 2017 at 12:37 am </a>
</span>
</footer>
<div class=3D"mh-comment-content">
<p>Accidentals simply raise or lower the pitch of the note by a half step f=
rom what is in the key signature. They last for the rest of the measure (un=
less another accidental is used). Sharps raise the pitch by a half step. Fl=
ats lower the pitch by a half step. Naturals remove a sharp or flat for the=
 rest of the measure.</p>
</div>
